.TH BALAI-CHAT 1 "2026" "BalOS 1.0" "BalOS Manual"
.SH NAME
balai-chat \- graphical Qt6 front-end for BalAI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B balai-chat
[\fIquestion\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A PySide6 chat window around the same local Qwen2.5 model used by
.BR balai (1).
If one or more positional arguments are given, they are joined and
sent as the initial query as soon as the window appears — the entry
point used by the KRunner plugin (see
.BR balai-krunner (1)).

The window is divided in two:

.SS Sidebar (left)
Live system dashboard updated every 5 s. Reflects
.B /run/balos/power-profile
and
.B /run/balos/shield-tier
changes in real time via
.B QFileSystemWatcher
(no polling lag). Shows battery, AC, CPU load, governor, memory,
disk, iface, IPv4, SSID, VPN state, firewall tier, kernel, uptime.

.SS Chat (right)
Streaming message area with fenced-code rendering, plus a toolbar of
one-click actions (Doctor, Tip, Context, Remember, Copy code, Clear,
Stop) and a model dropdown populated from
.BR "ollama list" "."
.SH SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Enter
Send current message.
.TP
.B Shift+Enter
Newline in the input.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Clear the conversation.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Run
.BR "balai doctor" .
.TP
.B Ctrl+T
Run
.BR "balai tip" .
.TP
.B Ctrl+K
Show
.BR "balai ctx" .
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Export the current conversation to a markdown file.
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
Open the settings dialog (context mode / temperature / theme).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy the most recent fenced code block to the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit (really — bypasses the tray-hide behaviour).
.SH SYSTEM TRAY
If the desktop supports a tray, closing the window hides to tray
instead of quitting. Right-click offers Show/Hide, Ask…, Doctor,
Quit. Answers that arrive while hidden raise a desktop
notification with the first line of the response.
.SH SETTINGS
Persisted via
.B QSettings
under the
.B BalOS/balai-chat
namespace (backed by
.BR "~/.config/BalOS/balai-chat.conf" ).
Fields:
.BR ctx_mode " (auto/always/never),"
.BR temperature " (0.00-1.50),"
.BR theme "."
Changes to
.B ctx_mode
are exported to
.B BALAI_CTX_MODE
so the worker thread and any spawned
.B balai
subprocesses inherit them.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BALAI_MODEL
Default model, shown in the dropdown at start (user can switch).
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
host:port of the ollama daemon (default 127.0.0.1:11434).
.TP
.B BALAI_NOTES_FILE
Override the notes location (default
.BR "~/.local/state/balai/notes.md" ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR balai (1),
.BR balai-krunner (1),
.BR ollama (1)
